## Lazy SSH Connection Setup

The SSH connection is only made when a resource or data source of this provider is created, read, updated or deleted. The arguments of the provider can therefore be values that are only known after apply.

## Provider Override

Resources and data sources also accept the connection settings directly, in a `provider_override` block, as a workaround for dynamic providers. The block takes the same arguments as the provider plus an `id`, which is used for connection pooling and locking.

